        ]
      },
      "worked": "Bob did not recognise that $\\ln(\\frac{1}{5})$ is negative:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\ln\\left(\\frac15\\right)&=\\ln(5^{-1})\\\\\\ln\\left(\\frac15\\right)&=-\\ln(5).\\end{align*}$$\nHence his expression becomes\n$$\\begin{align*}t&=-\\frac{\\ln(1/5)}{\\ln(2)}\\\\t&=-\\frac{-\\ln(5)}{\\ln(2)}\\\\t&=\\frac{\\ln(5)}{\\ln(2)}>0.\\end{align*}$$\nBoth methods give the same positive time. Bob’s sign evaluation, rather than his algebraic expression, is the mistake.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
